From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:56:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] user32: tell windows and callbacks registered for power
 settings their values.

RegisterPowerSettingNotification handed back 0xdeadbeef and told
nothing.  Windows tells a registration the current value of its setting
soon after it is made, from another thread - a window by a sent
WM_POWERBROADCAST with PBT_POWERSETTINGCHANGE, a callback of
DEVICE_NOTIFY_CALLBACK by a call - and again whenever it changes.  Word
registers its windows for six settings as it starts.

Registrations are now real, and each is told what Windows tells:
the power source and the battery's charge as NtPowerInformation reads
them, the one power scheme there is, balanced, as the active scheme and
its personality, the monitor and the console display on, energy saver
off, and for the idle background task the DWORD 2 Windows sends, which
it says means nothing.  Away mode is never on, and like settings there
are none of and a battery that is not there, it is told nothing.  The
power source and the charge are looked at every five seconds while
anything is registered for them, and a change is told as it is seen.

What is refused is as on Windows: flags other than the three, a
suspend and resume registration for a service; a successful
registration sets the last error to 0, and unregistering NULL fails
with ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER.  A service is not told anything yet, and
a service status handle that is none is not refused, as Windows does
with ERROR_SERVICE_NOT_IN_EXE.  A callback is not called after
unregistering it returns; a window may still get what it was about to
be sent.

Suspend and resume registrations are real too, but Wine does not see
the system suspend, so they are never told anything.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit a1de13bdc54ec5fe238010d58d1b4666e5873940)

